> Trace the executed native model and count the actual leaves

The source creates input/W[3,3,1,16], input/b[16], row/W[1,3,4,16],
output/W[1,1,4,1] and output/b[1], in that order. Missing kernels use
normal(0,.1), biases zero, store seed8303. This is144+16+192+4+1=357 values in
five leaves. Mask A permits four of nine input-kernel cells, so80 input weights
are forbidden and277 values are active. There is no row/b or initial-state leaf.

The executed architecture collapses the eight true row transitions into one
composite sequence block. The preceding one-row method diagram and worked
transition expose its mechanics. The public API returns the actual zero-state,
input-gate, recurrent-gate, hidden, cell and logit boundaries, retaining their
first and higher derivative paths.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pr_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore p(8303);
 n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& x){
  auto out=n::models::PixelRnn(p,x);
  n::model_stage("Mask A input1 to16",x,out.input_gates);
  n::model_stage("Connected zero h and c",out.input_gates,out.initial_hidden);
  n::model_stage("Eight recurrent Row-LSTM steps",std::vector<n::Tensor>{out.input_gates,out.initial_hidden},out.hidden);
  return n::model_stage("1x1 hidden4 to binary logits",out.hidden,out.logits);
 },"One width4 Row LSTM:357 stored values");
 n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
 options.sizing.minimum_extent=2;options.sizing.max_planes=4;
 auto fig=model.plot(n::zeros({1,8,8,1}),options);
 if(fig.parameter_count()!=357||p.size()!=5)throw std::runtime_error("Source census");
 fig.save_svg("build/pr_network.svg");
}
